  "terminosYPrivacidad": "Terms and Privacy",
  "politicaDePrivacidad": "Privacy Policy",
  "politicaPrivacidadIntro": "Last updated: {fecha}\n\nWelcome to ATRIO (\"Live your Faith in community\"). We respect your privacy and are deeply committed to protecting your personal data and your spiritual journey.\n\nThis policy outlines how we collect, manage, protect, and safeguard your information.",
  "@politicaPrivacidadIntro": {
    "description": "Introduction to the privacy policy",
    "placeholders": {
      "fecha": { "type": "String" }
    }
  },
  "seccionInfoQueRecopilamos": "1. Information We Collect",
  "parrafoInfoQueRecopilamos": "• Account Data: When signing in or registering (email, Google Sign-In, or Apple ID), we securely store your name and email address.\n\n• Community and Profile Data: Phone number, Christian tradition, and church or community to which you are voluntarily linked to customize your church experience.\n\n• Local Device Storage: Your Bible study notes, favorite passages, personal settings, and browsing history are stored locally in SQLite. We do not share your private reflections with third parties.\n\n• Requests and Donations: We record the status of your prayer requests, pastoral inquiries, and donation or contribution receipts for solidarity projects to provide you with direct visibility and traceability.",
  "seccionUsoServiciosTerceros": "2. Use of Third-Party Services",
  "parrafoUsoServiciosTerceros": "Our platform integrates with trusted technologies to deliver full functionality:\n\n• Google Play Services, Google Sign-In, and Sign in with Apple (Authentication and security).\n\n• Google Maps Platform (For accurate geographic location of churches, parishes, and community events on the interactive map).\n\n• Secure Payment Gateways (For reliable and encrypted receipt of offerings, tithes, and solidarity contributions).\n\n• YouTube and Broadcast Streamers (For religious services, live events, and radio broadcasts).",
  "seccionRetencionYEliminacion": "3. Data Retention and Deletion",
  "parrafoRetencionYEliminacion": "We retain your account data while it remains active. In accordance with Apple App Store (5.1.1 v) and Google Play Console guidelines, you have an unconditional right to request the complete and permanent deletion of your account and personal data.\n\nYou can perform this action at any time using the \"Delete account and data\" option on the Profile screen, or by emailing soporte@atrioapp.com with the subject \"Account Deletion\".\n\nAll local SQLite records and backend associations will be permanently purged.",
  "seccionPermisosDelDispositivo": "4. Device Permissions",
  "parrafoPermisosDelDispositivo": "ATRIO only requests permissions strictly required for its operation:\n\n• Location (GPS): Only used when accessing the map to show nearby churches and events.\n\n• Internet and Network Access: To synchronize requests, view live broadcasts, and validate contributions.\n\n• Notifications: For reminders of liturgical services, community events, and responses to requests.",
  "terminosDeUsoTitulo": "Terms of Use",
  "parrafoTerminosDeUso": "1. Conduct and community respect: ATRIO is a digital space of fellowship, mutual edification, and support for church ministries. The use of defamatory, fraudulent, or disrespectful language is strictly prohibited.\n\n2. Biblical and multimedia content: Biblical texts, station broadcasts, and shared videos respect the copyrights of their respective entities and ministries. Commercial exploitation outside the platform is prohibited.\n\n3. Donations and contributions: Contributions made through ATRIO go directly to the selected religious communities and solidarity projects. The app acts as a transparent and secure facilitating bridge.",
  "aceptacionTerminosPoliticas": "By using ATRIO, you accept these terms and community guidelines.",
